BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The closest alternatives fall into three groups. Mail-order rental subscriptions offer large) Tj T* (catalogs but cost more per use, impose shipping windows, and are aimed at working adults.) Tj T* (General resale and peer-to-peer fashion apps have large audiences but optimize for permanent) Tj T* (ownership, not borrowing for a specific date, and offer no campus-level trust or fast pickup.) Tj T* (Informal channels, such as group chats and social media posts asking to borrow a dress, are) Tj T* (free and already common, which is evidence of demand, but they are unorganized, unreliable and) Tj T* (offer no protection if an item is damaged or never returned. Our advantage is that we serve the) Tj T* (exact moment students need an outfit, from people nearby whom they can verify, with payment and) Tj T* (protection built in. The main risk is that a larger platform adds a campus mode. We intend to) Tj T* (defend against this by building density on each campus first and by working with student) Tj T* (organizations, which creates relationships a general app will find hard to copy.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priya Raghunathan, chief executive, is a senior in business administration who ran the) Tj T* (formalwear closet for her sorority and observed the problem firsthand. She leads strategy,) Tj T* (partnerships and campus operations. Marcus Delacroix-Boyd, chief technology officer, is a) Tj T* (senior in computer science who built the first version of the app and previously completed two) Tj T* (summer internships in mobile development. Tamsin Okafor-Lindqvist, head of growth and design,) Tj T* (is a junior in marketing and design who led our user research and designed the brand and) Tj T* (listing experience. The team has complementary skills across operations, engineering and) Tj T* (growth, and has worked together for eight months.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have defined the core concept, registered the company, and launched a working version of the) Tj T* (app. In a six-week pilot on one campus, 187 students created accounts, 241 items were listed,) Tj T* (and 63 students completed paid rentals, generating 1,940 dollars in transaction volume and) Tj T* (about 291 dollars in fee revenue. Of renters, 44 percent completed a second rental within the) Tj T* (pilot window, and the average lender earned 37 dollars. Our costs to date are modest, covering) Tj T* (app store fees, hosting and printed materials, at roughly 2,400 dollars funded personally by) Tj T* (the founders. We have not yet formed a legal entity for the business and plan to do so with) Tj T* (legal support before taking any prize money. Our forecast for the next twelve months assumes) Tj T* (launch on four additional campuses, 3,500 registered users, 1,400 paid renters and about 55,000) Tj T* (dollars in transaction volume, producing roughly 9,000 dollars in fee revenue. We expect to) Tj T* (reach break-even on direct costs within a year and to fund growth from a mix of competition) Tj T* (prizes and a small seed round.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for prize funding of 25,000 dollars, mentorship from experienced marketplace and) Tj T* (consumer app founders, and help with legal formation and trust and safety policy. The funds) Tj T* (would be allocated roughly as follows: 10,000 dollars for engineering time to add in-app) Tj T* (payments, damage protection and verified student onboarding; 9,000 dollars for launch marketing) Tj T* (and student ambassador programs on four campuses; 4,000 dollars for legal formation, insurance) Tj T* (and terms of service; and 2,000 dollars for operating costs. With this support we aim to prove) Tj T* (that the model repeats across campuses and to be ready for a seed round after the next formal) Tj T* (season.) Tj ET
